Reviewed through `59b5eca`, read-only. Most corrections are accurate; four documentation issues remain.

1. **O5 — The dtype explanation still conflates two decisions.** [results.md:108](/Users/poonszesen/kg-v3/ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/results.md:108) attributes the all-buffer storage-size check to template size arguments. That check selects emitted `INDEX_DTYPE`; the separate `SIMDKernelFeatures([], output_numel)` path determines size-argument dtype using output numel. Correct this distinction and the corresponding [Reference wording](/Users/poonszesen/kg-v3/cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:44).

2. **O7 — A new attribution overclaim was introduced.** The [Reference:30](/Users/poonszesen/kg-v3/cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:30) says “Every failing graph launches” an i32 template; [results.md:113](/Users/poonszesen/kg-v3/ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/results.md:113) similarly claims agreement with every failing graph. The 768→256 and 512→256 failures during autotuning do not identify the precise faulting candidate. Narrow these statements to attributable retained kernels and explicitly preserve that localization gap.

3. **O11 — The run statement retains an unsupported installed-version assertion.** [Run statement:16](/Users/poonszesen/kg-v3/ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/run-statements/gemm-limits-probe.md:16) still names Triton 3.5.0 without qualification. Match the corrected results: **3.5.0 is the lockfile pin; the installed version was not captured.**

4. **B2/O9 — Two boundary notations need reconciliation.** [Reference:28](/Users/poonszesen/kg-v3/cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:28) needs `floor(2³¹/K)` for `L_in`; the 768 quotient is fractional. Its [design bound at line 48](/Users/poonszesen/kg-v3/cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:48) says `≤2³¹`, while the implemented and prescribed conservative admission rule is `<2³¹`. Use the strict rule, or explicitly distinguish the inferred equality allowance from the unmeasured real-trunk endpoint.

